1412e26":"Weekend classes","9e38e0e189":"Listed for its weekend classes","a464b2ae90":"It hasn’t listed dates we can chart.","d7223a112b":"Listed for its day camps","8e1551a650":"Tell me when something changes","bb10979102":"One email before sign-ups open at {camp}, if it names a day, and one when its dates or prices change.","e30e2ee39e":"We’ve only read up on its weekend classes so far, so it isn’t on any school’s page.","48bdbd1d28":"Find or book a spot","d1a9ac541a":"We’ve only read up on its camps on days off so far, so it isn’t on any school’s page.","6b7cb8066c":"Weeks it runs in {year}","36f240972c":"Each box is a week, named by its Monday.","af124f321b":"1 more break","35ed632c9c":"Some of this came from the program itself, on {date}.","8c6b37a4ff":"Start from where you live. Each neighborhood lists the schools there, the after-school programs, weekend classes, day camps and summer camps based there, and the programs that come to pick up.","1a4b3e864c":"A program is listed where its building is. Many pick up from schools in other neighborhoods, so your school’s page is still the fullest list.","c90125477b":"Don’t see your neighborhood?","07ede3f675":"Tell us which school or program to add.","d09357da10":"Weekend classes, by part of the city","b8d4acdd17":"Saturday and Sunday classes aren’t tied to a school, so they’re listed by where they are.","ee9aa9711a":"All neighborhoods","f7e8f609f9":"{name}: after school, weekends and camps","100b7b0642":"The schools in {name}, and everything listed here or coming to pick up: after-school programs, weekend classes, day camps and summer camps.","bbb2092610":"Schools in {name}","21f158fdb0":"Based in {name}. Each one shows the schools it serves; open it for hours, cost and how to register.","3cb37ac44e":"Saturday and Sunday classes go by where they are. Any child can sign up, whichever school they go to.","e682dce797":"Camps on the days district schools are closed, based in {name}. Children from any school can go.","2e224fe2e8":"Summer day camps with a site in {name}.","bc2cbd42ce":"Based elsewhere, but they pick up here","59e4b197e5":"These programs are in another neighborhood and collect children from a school in {name}.","dc1cdaca15":"Weekend classes close by, in {area}","9714dc4d38":"All weekend classes in {area}","32441257e2":"Other neighborhoods","dac2a8fa8c":"No school in {name} is on the site yet.","cb175bd67a":"Ask for yours.","0aad960705":"Any amount. It opens a Stripe checkout page, which takes cards, Apple Pay and Google Pay, and sends you a receipt.","f6308fefdc":"Help the site keep going","0e51d4c4c4":"{site} is free for families, and it will stay that way. It isn’t free to run. If it saved you an evening of open tabs, you can chip in toward what it costs to keep it going and growing.","6b50e31a7e":"Thank you","43d3d21d35":"Your contribution went through, and a receipt is on its way to the email you gave. It goes straight to keeping the site running. Thank you for helping it keep going.","2a305d6af3":"Your monthly contribution is set up, and a receipt is on its way to the email you gave; one comes each month it goes through. It goes straight to keeping the site running. To change or stop it, email {email} any time. Thank you for helping it keep going.","4e3e991222":"It goes toward what the site costs to run: web hosting, the service that sends sign-in codes and date reminders, and the hours spent checking listings and adding schools.","5429d9e1bb":"It goes through Stripe to {operator}, the small company the Silverbauers set up to run the site and pay its bills.","a6e5445ec9":"It’s a contribution to a small family-run project, not a charitable donation, so it isn’t tax-deductible.","54559419a5":"It buys nothing on the site. Listings are free for every provider, and nobody pays to be listed or to be listed higher.","8d1835ee55":"Can’t chip in? A correction or a missing program helps just as much.","6d85a0da52":"Send one here.","3da90473e4":"Privacy, in plain English","adcf19af19":"This site is run by one parent. It collects as little as it can. Here is what it does collect, where it goes, and how to have it removed.","f7dd5c66e9":"The short version","3450783a88":"There are no ads, and nothing you send is sold. Looking things up needs no account. The planners (the week, the days off, the summer and the calendar) need a free one, and an account is also for following a program’s dates, keeping favorites, keeping your school or a plan in a profile, and sharing a week with someone.","1c49804aa1":"Your rosters, including any child’s name you type, are saved in your own browser. While you are signed in, a week that has a first name and a program on it is also kept in your profile, so it is there on your other devices. You can take it out of your profile, and it then stays in your browser only. Nobody else sees a week unless you share it.","66b0cd85db":"If you send a suggestion or a review, it arrives as an email to the person who runs the site.","e9b299f5d2":"If you follow a program, a camp or a school, the list of what you follow is kept in your account, and your email address and that list are kept by Klaviyo, the service that sends the emails.","5209da1bbe":"If you ask for a school that isn’t covered yet, that uses your account: which school you asked for is kept with it, so each family counts once. Klaviyo keeps your email address, your name if you’ve given it, and which school you’re waiting for, so you can be told when it has its page.","f844260e06":"We use Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to see how the site is used, so we can fix what’s confusing.","63e8b54c61":"Rosters and children’s names","5c228fe5c0":"A roster lives in the browser you made it in. Clearing your browser’s site data deletes it.","04e0346c61":"A summer schedule and a days-off plan are kept the same way: your picks, and any first name you type, are saved in your browser and, while you are signed in, in your profile. You can take either out of your profile, and it then stays in your browser only. A photo you add to a calendar picture is used once, in your browser, and is never saved or uploaded.","b7dac40b19":"If you save a school as yours, that choice is kept in your own browser too. Our visit counts record that a school was saved, not who saved it.","4bdd32c9ec":"A child’s name is optional, and a nickname or an initial works. A week with no name on it stays on your device. A name you do add is kept in your profile with the plan it is on, and goes with a week you share.","40afaccc40":"Dates you add yourself to “My kids’ calendar”, like picture day or a form that’s due, are kept in your browser and nowhere else. They are not sent to us and are not part of your profile, so they don’t appear on your other devices.","72d228d3ed":"A week can no longer be shared as a link. A link showed the week to anyone who had it and could not be taken back, so links made before October 2026 have stopped opening.","2d3a826155":"If one of those older links is opened, the site still removes the name from the page address before any analytics loads. The roster page is set to be hidden in session recordings.","82b70f14b8":"Making a card happens on your own device. What you do with the picture is up to you.","2e3b852749":"If you add a photo to a week card, the card is made in your own browser. The photo is not uploaded, not saved, and gone when you close the page.","069e85c867":"Accounts, profiles and sharing","b5f33af957":"An account is free. The lists and listings are open to everyone; the planners need you to sign in. The plans you make while signed in (a child’s week, the days off, the summer) are kept in your profile, so they are on every device you sign in on, and you can take any of them out. An account also lets you keep your school in your profile, share a week with one person, and join a share group of a few families who know each other. Your profile, a shared week and a group are the only parts of the site that keep anything about a child on our server.","ec48d4711a":"An account is an email address and your first and last name. The email signs you in and tells you when someone opens a week you shared or joins a group you made. Other members never see it.","03d53fc3b9":"When an account is made, the person who runs this site gets an email with the account’s name and email address, and, for a program manager, the listing they claimed. Nothing about a child is in that email.","c93b335047":"You can change the email address on your account, from your account page. We send a code to the new address to check that it’s yours. Once you type it in, you sign in with the new address, what you follow moves to it on the email list, a short note goes to the old address, and your other devices are signed out. The old address is no longer on your account, but it stays on our email list until it is unsubscribed: use the Unsubscribe link in any email, or ask us and we’ll remove it.","72a0cd17f3":"You can sign in with Google instead of an emailed code. Google’s button is loaded on the pages where you sign in, so Google can see that someone opened that page. If you use it, Google tells us your name and email address. We ask for nothing else and never see your Google password.","311e526c3d":"If you keep your school in your profile, we store which school. If you keep your children’s grades or ages, we store the grades and ages and nothing about which child is which. An age you give a child on the summer planner is kept with your profile’s ages the same way. For a week in your profile, we store the child’s first name, the programs on their current and upcoming weeks, and the school each program was picked under, so the week can be put back on another device. Notes you type are not stored.","26087fec93":"For a summer schedule in your profile, we store each child’s first name as you typed it and the camps picked for each week, so the summer is there on your other devices. The calendar’s title and photos are not stored. A summer in your profile can’t be shared with anyone, and it is deleted when you take it out of your profile or delete your account. The summer schedule section is hidden in session recordings, and analytics is told only that a summer was kept, never what is in it.","21b3fc24af":"For a days-off plan in your profile, we store each child’s first name as you typed it, the place picked for each day school is closed, and which of those days you ticked as signed up. The calendar’s title and photos are not stored. The plan can’t be shared with anyone, and it is deleted when you take it out of your profile or delete your account. The planner is hidden in session recordings, and analytics is never told what is in a plan.","47055568c5":"“My kids’ calendar” is drawn in your browser, for you alone, from the plans on your device and the ones in your profile. Opening it stores nothing new and sends nothing about your plans. It has no link of its own, so nobody else can open it. A picture or calendar file you save is a copy on your device that we never receive. So it can tell you when a date changes, the page remembers what your last file held, on your device only. Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity are not loaded on it.","b97f9e1314":"Sharing a week with one person sends an invitation to the address you give. It only opens for someone signed in with that address, they can look and print but not change anything, and you can take it back at any time.","036b101d10":"Making an account also adds your name and email to our email list, kept by Klaviyo, for occasional news about the site. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing does not affect your account.","13665fd8b1":"The email list also notes whether an account belongs to a parent or to someone who manages a program, so each gets only the news meant for them. For a manager it notes the name of the listing they hold.","d8fff29c03":"A new account is asked for a first and last name, and may add a school and a neighborhood. The school and neighborhood set where lists start, and they are noted on the email list so news can be about where you are. Both are optional, and you can change or clear them on your account page.","bc24286560":"Once you have signed in, this device remembers one word, “parent” or “manager”. On the pages that load analytics, that word is passed along so we can count the two groups separately. Your name, your email address and anything in your profile are not.","61b57a197b":"There are no passwords. We email you a link and a 6-digit code; each works once and for 15 minutes. A cookie then keeps that device signed in for 30 days, and you can sign out everywhere from your account page.","f04d299ecb":"When you add a week to a group, we store the child’s first name as you type it and the programs on their current and upcoming weeks. We do not store a last name, school, address, pickup time, note, teacher’s name, photo, price or day-off plan.","837ce2621f":"Nobody can find a group or ask to join one. The person who made it invites email addresses, and only someone signed in with an invited address, who also has the code from the invitation, gets in. A group isn’t listed anywhere, and its link shows nothing to anyone else.","32b6a5ac52":"If someone invites you, they give us your email address so we can send the invitation and recognise you if you join. We keep it with that group, use it for nothing else, and delete it when you are removed or the group ends. The invitation shows the name and email of the person who invited you.","0e7432357e":"A group’s creator sees the name and email address of each adult in it; other members don’t.","0a4f76533e":"Someone who joins to view only, such as a caregiver, can see and print the group and cannot change it.","dc603f7563":"Anyone in a group can print it or take a screenshot, so keep groups to people you know and would tell where your child is anyway.","2c5371e59c":"Accounts, profiles and groups are kept in a file on our web host, outside the public site. Google Analytics, Microsoft Clarity and Klaviyo’s script are not loaded on your account page, your profile page, on invitations or on group pages. Two pages around them do load them. The page where you create an account counts visits: its form is hidden in session recordings, and analytics is told only that a sign-up started, whether it used email or Google, and that it finished, never the address or a name. The Build your week page is hidden in session recordings too, and analytics is told only that something was kept or shared, never what or with whom.","31cbf618a5":"The emails the site itself sends, such as sign-in codes, invitations and notices about a listing, are delivered by Postmark, an email delivery service. It is given the address and the message so it can deliver them, and it keeps a record of each one for a limited time so delivery problems can be traced. We have its tracking of opens and clicks turned off for these emails.","5cf52c2db8":"Postmark’s privacy policy","fa3a27cb62":"We keep a daily count of how many accounts, shared weeks and groups were made, to see whether this is used. The counts hold no names, addresses or weeks.","a469bdc578":"You can take a week out of your profile or out of a group, stop sharing, leave a group, or delete your account from the site at any time, and it is removed straight away. A group’s creator can remove anyone. Every shared week and group is deleted two weeks after the last day of school.","35a4be5cea":"A safety copy of the accounts database is made each day and kept for 14 days, in case something breaks, and our web host keeps its own backups. So what you delete is gone from the site straight away, and leaves those copies as they are replaced, usually within a month.","ff84e08097":"Accounts are for parents, caregivers, teachers and the people who run programs. Children should not make one. The planners are for the adult who signs in, and a child’s name on a plan is optional.","de5ce68b78":"If you manage a program and claim its listing","3905d8d8ab":"Claiming uses the same account. We check one thing: that the email address you signed in with is at the listing’s own website address. We keep which listing you claimed, when, and whether the claim stands.","db601ebc70":"The public sees a “Claimed” mark on the listing and nothing about you. Your name and email address are seen only by the person who runs this site.","b6e4209068":"If you hold a listing, we email you about it: its numbers once a month, a note when a review of it is published, and a note when more families start following it. You can turn these off on the managers page or from a link in any of them.","2e87e86e32":"What a program’s managers are told about families is numbers only: how many times a listing was opened, and how many families started following it. Never who.","352fda9fb8":"Changes you propose are kept with your claim and emailed to the site’s inbox. They are checked and published by a person, and you are told by email when that happens.","aeca6ded55":"A photo you send for your listing is shrunk in your browser before it leaves your device, kept on our web host, and shown on the listing only after a person approves it. You can replace or remove it at any time. Send only a photo you have the right to use, with permission from the families of any children in it.","8a47cce210":"A premium listing can also carry a logo, a section in your own words and an offer or event line. Each is kept on our web host with your claim, read by a person before it shows, and marked on the listing as coming from the program. You can change or remove any of them at any time.","c8467ed42b":"If you sign a listing up for premium, we keep which plan you picked and the day you picked it, with your claim. It goes when the claim or the account does.","5bd35e9485":"A premium listing is paid for on Stripe’s own page. Your card details go to Stripe and never reach us. Stripe tells us who paid, how much and for which listing, so we can switch it on. When Stripe sends you back here, the page tells our visitor statistics that a sale was made and for which plan, not who made it.","9134b2fa26":"A question a parent sends from your listing comes to the email address on your account, and to anyone else who holds the listing, with the parent’s address to reply to. We pass it along and don’t keep a copy.","550d83b376":"If you say whether there’s space, the listing shows “Spots open”, “Waitlist” or “Full” and the day you said it. It goes up at once, without anyone checking it, and comes down after 30 days unless you set it again.","4a55bb4633":"You can give up a claim at any time, and deleting your account removes your claims and the changes you proposed.","7d5d4993dc":"The page where you claim a listing loads Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to count visits. The part where you sign in and manage claims is hidden in session recordings.","7f8f847dc5":"Suggestions, corrections and reviews","6cc5cdc188":"What you type into a form is emailed to the site’s inbox, and a backup copy is kept on our web host in case the email goes missing.","94f7d60f5b":"Your email address is used only to reply to you or to confirm something. It is never published.","0e0b3194ab":"A review that is approved appears on the site with your first name, your child’s school and the month. Nothing else about you is shown.","24df0236d2":"When a program has been on your week for a few weeks, the site may ask whether you’d review it. That is worked out in your browser, from the rosters on your device. Your device remembers the day it first saw each program on a roster, when it last asked, and which programs you reviewed or said not to ask about. None of that is sent to us, and “Don’t ask about this one” ends it for that program.","cc67baee23":"If you are signed in, the review form fills in your first name and email address from your account so you don’t have to type them. You can change either before you send it.","73569b8eed":"Asking for a school to be covered sends only the school’s name.","410ec9d6bb":"A date you send in for a school’s page (picture day, a half day) is read by a person before it is published. What is published is the date and what it is, marked “from a parent”: never your name or email.","b9fb0bfae2":"Please don’t include children’s names or other people’s personal details in what you send.","32fd0857ff":"Some listings have an “Ask a question” button. What you type there, with your first name and email address, is emailed to the people who run that program so they can answer you. We pass it along and don’t keep a copy. We do count that a question was asked.","f9dda5e549":"Distances and the map","a81063878a":"“From where I am” asks your browser for your location. It is used on your device to work out distances, it is not sent to us, and it is not kept.","5320f4f2ab":"The map stays off until you tap “Show the map”. Its pictures then come from OpenStreetMap’s servers, which see your internet address and which part of the city you looked at, as any website you visit does.","be62daa255":"OpenStreetMap’s privacy policy","f8bbcf6d58":"Distances are measured in a straight line from street addresses, so a walk is usually a little longer.","d4819c397f":"Dates by email","bfa195ba5e":"Following a program, a camp or a school uses a free account. Your account keeps the list of what you follow. Your browser sends two things to Klaviyo, the email service we use: your email address (with your first name, if your account has one) and what you follow. They are stored there.","89e3f216a1":"You hear only about what you follow. Stop following from the listing’s page or from your account page and those emails stop; deleting your account stops them all.","9e323f99bf":"A sign-up date is emailed the morning after it is posted on this site, with reminders the day before and on the morning itself. Days off come in a weekly round-up. We can only pass on a date once the program has posted it and it has reached this site.","70f6347d02":"Every date email has a link for each listing in it, “Stop emails about …”. It stops that one listing without signing in, including its dates that would have reached you through a school you follow, and you can undo it on the spot or from your account page.","b07c8e2d3a":"That link works because it carries a random code that belongs to your account. The code is kept with your account and on your email-list profile, and it can do one thing: stop emails. It can’t open your account or show anything in it, and the page it opens never says whose it is.","facb309ae3":"So that a stop always holds, we keep a list of what has been stopped in a scrambled form that can’t be read back into a person or a listing without that code. The entry for a deleted account stays on that list, so its emails stay stopped.","ae7b754175":"“This week at your school” is an email you turn on in your account, for the school kept there. It is off until you tick it. It works like following: which school it is for is kept in your account and on your email-list profile, and you can turn it off there or from the link in any of those emails.","505b35a201":"A favorite is different. It is kept in your account and nowhere else: it isn’t sent to Klaviyo, and it sends no email.","3c99f627a5":"Notifications on your phone or computer are optional, and off until you turn them on from your account page. When you do, your browser gives us an address at its own notification service (Google’s for Chrome and Android, Apple’s for Safari and iPhones, Mozilla’s for Firefox) and two keys. We keep those with your account and use them only to send you the dates for what you follow. Each notification is sealed so that the notification service carrying it can’t read it. Turning notifications off on a device removes that device, and deleting your account removes them all.","1b48cd898a":"If you choose notifications instead of the date emails, those emails stop while one of your devices can still get notifications, and start again by themselves if none can.","2f37bba10a":"A phone number is optional. If you add one and tick the box agreeing to texts, we keep the number, the day you agreed and the wording you agreed to, in your account. It is for texts about what you follow and nothing else. Texts have not started yet; until they do, the number is not passed to any texting service. You can remove it on your account page at any time, and a text will always say how to stop them. Message and data rates may apply.","10bf823f58":"Asking to be told when a school is added still takes only a first name and an email address, with no account.","0f1b0b26a2":"It never asks for a child’s name, grade or anything else about your family, and your roster is not sent with it.","02b0e18b5d":"Like most email services, Klaviyo records whether an email was opened and which links were clicked, and it may estimate a general location from your internet connection.","1e3d45d7f9":"Your name and address are used for these date emails and nothing else. They are not shared with the programs listed here, and they are not sold.","77b9ae4735":"The same goes for a phone number.","3c33892438":"Every email has an unsubscribe link, and using it stops the emails. To have your name and address deleted altogether, email us.","02b6a17db4":"Klaviyo handles that data under its own terms:","a1f21c2fb6":"Klaviyo’s privacy notice","13514871d2":"Counts for each listing","45ed82b34e":"We keep a count, for each listing and each day, of how many times its page was opened, how many times its sign-up and website links were followed, how many times it was put on a plan, and how many people asked for its emails.","cda58d2245":"If your browser has a school saved when you open a listing’s page, we also add one to a monthly count for that school, so the people who run the listing can see which schools’ families are looking. What is kept is which school is saved and a number: nothing about who you are.","679564089a":"It is a number and nothing else. No cookie is set, and nothing says who you are, which child a plan was for, or what else you looked at.","05cd22fdf7":"To stop a count being run up, the server keeps a scrambled form of the internet address behind each count for up to two days. It can’t be turned back into the address and isn’t tied to what was counted.","19c20a17d0":"The people who run a listing they have claimed can see that listing’s numbers. Nobody else can, apart from us.","77a09c8b1d":"Analytics and recordings","44d34909fd":"Google Analytics records which pages are visited and which buttons, filters and searches are used, along with general details such as device type and approximate location. That includes the words typed into the program search box.","c4da07c2ab":"Microsoft Clarity records how pages are used, including heatmaps and replays of scrolling and clicking, to help us improve the site. We have set it to hide form fields and the roster page.","c91906cce4":"Klaviyo, the email service, also has a small script on the public pages. It sets a cookie so that a visit that started from one of its emails can be tied to that address, and it records which pages that visit saw. It is not loaded on the pages listed above either.","f697ee2552":"These services use cookies and similar technologies, and Google, Microsoft and Klaviyo handle that data under their own privacy terms:","04cb347cfe":"how Google uses information from sites that use its services","664944bb97":"the Microsoft Privacy Statement","fc540cbede":"You can block all of them with your browser’s privacy settings or a content blocker, and the site will still work.","abba3c955f":"Like every website, our host keeps standard server logs, which include IP addresses.","bf541a9940":"Links to other sites","02412a3892":"Program websites, registration pages, calendars and Stripe’s checkout pages are run by other organizations and have their own privacy practices.","d6a9374e67":"Links to a program’s own site carry a short tag saying the visit came from {site}, and from which school’s page. The tag says nothing about you.","dcf75191c5":"Children","5677caacfb":"This site is written for parents and caregivers. It is not meant to be used by children, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.","e9d0974c5f":"Seeing or removing what you sent","39a1146667":"To have a review taken down, your email address removed from the date emails, or a suggestion and your contact details deleted, email","30beaab727":". Say what you sent and roughly when, and it will be removed.","b149e0bbf0":"Last updated {date}. If this page changes in a way that matters, the date changes with it.","183f016fc2":"The rules for using this site, in plain English. Using the site means you agree to them.","a0ab6ffd0e":"What this site is","51a6b83435":"{site} is a free directory. It gathers what after-school programs, weekend classes and camps in Philadelphia say about themselves on their own websites, and arranges it by school and neighborhood.","e4ef70c738":"{site} is run by {who}, a Pennsylvania limited liability company. “We” and “us” in these terms mean {who}.","3359d937ed":"We don’t run any of the programs listed, and we aren’t a child care provider, a school, a booking service or an agent for any program.","a45f772f57":"A listing is not a recommendation. We don’t inspect programs, check licences or insurance, run background checks on staff, or verify that a program is safe or right for your child.","ccb31de7db":"Hours, prices, dates, pickup routes and openings change, and what’s here can be out of date or wrong. Confirm everything with the program before you enroll, pay or rely on a pickup.","5c3a3567e1":"Choosing a program, and arranging how your child gets there and home, is your decision and your responsibility.","127d997818":"Who can use it","7a87c2d540":"The site is for adults: parents, guardians, caregivers and the people who run programs. Accounts are for people 18 and over. Children should not make an account or send us anything.","6f8cecd6f7":"If you make an account, use your own email address and your real name, and keep access to that email to yourself. You are responsible for what’s done from your account.","a8cc41044a":"Children’s information","497fdc2b5b":"Looking things up works without telling us anything about a child. A plan you make while signed in is kept in your profile, and you can share a week: you decide what first name to use, and you can use a nickname or an initial.","0d85524c8e":"Only add a child you are the parent or guardian of, or have that person’s permission to add.","e86e60b5ce":"What we store, and how to delete it, is on the privacy page.","15acae6ff2":"Read the privacy page.","9531476199":"Sharing a week, and groups","d406914b77":"When you share a week or start a group, you choose who sees it. We send the invitation to the email address you give and check that the person signs in with that address. We don’t know who they are beyond that, and we don’t screen anyone.","1e2c1717ca":"Only invite people you know and would tell where your child is anyway. Anyone you invite can print or screenshot what they see.","6e74d43811":"What happens between you and other people you meet or connect with through the site is between you and them. That includes carpools, shared pickups, playdates, babysitting and money. We are not a party to those arrangements and are not responsible for them.","d812cc1988":"You can stop sharing, leave a group or delete your account at any time.","0fa32ace54":"Reviews, suggestions and corrections","dc76296211":"A review should be your own first-hand experience, honest, and about the program rather than a named person. Don’t include children’s names or anyone’s private details.","30cf27f5e1":"We read reviews before they are posted, and we may shorten one, decline it or take it down. A review is the opinion of the person who wrote it, not ours.","b79a1e6de0":"By sending a review, suggestion or correction you let us publish it on the site and use it to improve the listings. You keep the rights to what you wrote.","fc4343257d":"If you run a program","a204462fcf":"Listings are free. We build them from your public website, and you can ask us to correct or remove one at any time.","c0616d13bf":"Claim a listing only if you work for that program and are allowed to speak for it. What you send us about it must be accurate and yours to share.","9d4227a64a":"Changes you propose are read before they go on the site. We may edit them to fit the page, decline them, or remove a claim.","ebff6cfde3":"A listing doesn’t make us your partner, agent or advertiser, and we don’t promise it will bring enrollments.","1d6ae60b32":"What’s not allowed","dd6ba10970":"Don’t use the site to harass anyone, to pretend to be someone else, or to collect information about children or families.","eb2fd2d272":"Don’t copy the listings in bulk to republish or sell them, and don’t try to break, overload or get around the site’s protections.","0ca4da443f":"We can suspend an account or remove content that breaks these rules.","08ad01556f":"Links and other services","dd480ef7a2":"The site links to programs’ own websites and sign-up pages. Those are theirs: their terms, prices and privacy practices apply there, and anything you buy or sign is between you and them.","d3ea60feaa":"Program names and logos belong to their owners. The rest of the site, including how the listings are written and arranged, is ours. You’re welcome to link to any page and to share the cards and calendars you make.","0bf64a9ab3":"No guarantees, and limits on our responsibility","19e569432c":"The site is provided as it is, free of charge, without any promise that it is complete, accurate, available or free of errors.","fc69e6d047":"As far as the law allows, {who} is not liable for loss or harm that comes from using the site, from relying on a listing, from a program you chose, or from your dealings with other people who use the site.","b4ec815cd0":"Nothing here limits any right you have that the law doesn’t allow to be limited.","f34c6e92f6":"Changes, and how to reach us","46a3253764":"We may change the site or these terms. When the terms change in a way that matters, the date below changes with them. If you keep using the site after that, the new terms apply.","a0c6aa03e7":"These terms are governed by the laws of Pennsylvania.","b112525712":"Questions about any of this:","83cf17eadd":"Last updated {date}.","d34fd34411":"One place to see what’s possible after the last bell","f6cc4005b7":"Finding after-school care means checking a dozen websites to learn who picks up from your school, for which grades, until when. {site} puts that on one page per school.","5b2fc57ac3":"How listings are checked","eb164ad365":"Each listing comes from the provider’s own public pages, the school’s site, or city program data. The sources are linked on every card.","3538dbc094":"Every card shows the date it was last checked. When a detail could not be confirmed, the card says so in a yellow note.","168197886b":"A program is marked “picks up” only when a source names the school. Otherwise it is listed as nearby.","e6927cf2fc":"What this site can’t promise","339b87f81a":"A listing is not an endorsement, and nobody pays to appear here.","02366fc9d1":"Prices, hours, openings and pickup routes change during the year. Confirm with the provider before you enroll.","116a91ada2":"{site} is independent. It is not affiliated with the School District of Philadelphia or any provider.","a7d376eed1":"How programs are sorted","19a9b8c07a":"At the school","b78b2d867a":"Runs in the school building or on its grounds. No travel.","c5898fc305":"Picks up","f1536c3517":"Nearby","abbbbdb7e3":"Close to the school, with no pickup we could find. A fit for older children or a second stop.","4ec0a4ca4b":"Every listing is dated and sourced","1a2e23c6b6":"Every listing links to where the information came from and shows the day it was last checked. Nobody pays to be listed. If it saved you an evening of open tabs,","859b47a3f7":"help the site keep going.","eb84427331":"Corrections, new programs and new schools","ba49970512":"Parents and providers know these programs best. If something is wrong or missing, or you want your school added,","67b96d067d":"use the form","6802c83437":"It helps to include the program, the school, what changed, and a link to where it’s published.","b83c4cdafe":"Reviews","5016c0caf6":"Reviews are first-hand notes from parents and caregivers. Each one is read before it’s posted and shows the reviewer’s first name and school.","98f6814b72":"We don’t post reviews that name children or individual staff, or reviews a program writes about itself.","db5ef27989":"Nobody pays to have a review posted or removed. A provider who thinks a review is wrong can use the form above or the contact address.","24463c5f78":"Who built this","42a9e2358a":"Josh Silverbauer is a parent of two, with one enrolled in Nebinger. Navigating after-school programs was chaos for him, so he figured it was chaos for everyone else too. His wife Rachael told him to stop complaining and build something. So he built this site. He then showed Rachael and she said “Brilliant! But the copy sucks,” so he said stop complaining and write something, so she wrote this site.","b96da3e11a":"Know one we missed?","3625d54ad4":"Plenty of good programs are off the radar: a church basement, a dance studio that walks kids over, a summer camp nobody has listed. Tell us and we’ll check it and add it. You can also send an update to a listing or ask for your school.","7c2fa947f6":"What are you sending?","06a83f5cdf":"The neighborhood helps too, if you know it.","6c52a3d661":"Which school?","1d2a2ff758":"For another school, name it in the details.","6200bb936f":"What kind of camp?","61acb05fb4":"Does it pick up from the school?","5c4698b6e0":"About you","d3f3c1b887":"All optional. Your email is only used to ask a follow-up question about what you sent.","b687c2eb73":"How we handle it.","f175d577f0":"How do you know it?","ab42293e29":"Your name","3fa6f5fb50":"Your email","51ecc5b21f":"What happens next","28af69d2cd":"Your note lands in a real inbox. A person reads it.","e836e8414a":"We check it against the program’s own information.","4a6923b699":"If it holds up, it goes on the site with its source and the date.","9fce963f8e":"Nothing is published automatically, and nobody pays to be listed.","41ace7cd55":"Run the program yourself?","fded9d2abb":"Claim your listing with your work email and send changes as its manager.","ee9ab1a21f":"How claiming works","815ecd6d02":"Got it. Thank you.","b3777a47d8":"We’ll check it against the program’s own information and add it if it holds up.","10b494ae4f":"Back to the schools.","7a304f2967":"What should this site do next?","ece8c308ad":"A missing filter, something confusing, a thing you wish it did. One person builds this, and reads every one.","fbcc6b1a22":"Your idea","93c7452449":"What were you trying to do, and what would have made it easier?","32861acdae":"Your name (optional)","2b9e323f35":"Only used to ask a follow-up question.","5aa549ca95":"Send the idea","2f86a867fa":"Other things you can send","e6595d151a":"A program that’s missing, or a correction","a5839cf3a1":"A school you want covered","7253574d81":"A review of a program your child went to","5bbf44b373":"Ideas get read, and the ones that help the most families get built first.","21bec4e65a":"Back to the start.","c49bb4c242":"Get in touch","3801bea586":"A question, a problem with the site, something for the press, or just hello. This goes to the parent who runs the site.","19aad2a493":"So we can write back. It’s used for nothing else.","49d97c7a8e":"What’s it about?","f190c98ece":"Your message","dd705eff4c":"Other ways","84add5b295":"Email","ec4e916f64":"A program or camp that’s missing, or a listing that’s wrong:","52e582dc06":"use the suggestion form","f240b9c8ed":", so it reaches the right pile.","36bf5af840":"An idea for the site:","edfe97bc23":"request a feature","3efdf3b227":"You run a program:","27c911bccd":"claim your listing","4a5bb991f2":"One parent reads these, usually within a few days.","0c5a112d4f":"How we handle what you send.","b3d4ce50d0":"Sent. Thank you.","da79c88a05":"Your message is in the inbox. You’ll hear back by email, usually within a few days.","82a8bb5146":"Build your week","b8b650bf6a":"Monday might be martial arts and Thursday the rec center. Plan the term that’s coming, keep a second roster for what your child is doing now, and send either to your partner, a sitter, or the group chat. More than one child? Each gets their own.","f95aa00b8e":"Free, with no password to remember: we email you a code, or you use Google.","156a225ed6":"On your phone and your computer","c442a449bf":"Signed in, your plan is in your profile, so it’s there on every device.","9dbb10d6e2":"The week builder","890fa3e8d9":"See the whole week before it starts","463051f7f3":"The week","0f01ed56a1":"Example","fe4033cd0a":"Not planned yet","f959f892f4":"Sam’s week","a857576e07":"Each child gets their own week. It adds up what the week costs, and makes one picture to text to a sitter.","1ebb12d59a":"Put a program on each afternoon, with its hours and when to pick up. Each child gets a week of their own.","9dc41758f2":"Budget planning","3e8a033fa1":"What Sam’s week comes to","c867070fff":"Half a school year","99edbf6738":"18 weeks of school","309da936bb":"An estimate from each program’s published prices. It leaves out fees, discounts and financial aid.","3379979b9b":"The week adds itself up from each program’s published prices, so you see the half-year before you sign up for anything.","5c41f87a30":"Share it","10e10b6a91":"One picture to send","a406db433f":"Text it to a sitter or the group chat","e641623ed9":"Print it for the fridge or a teacher","9cdc921cc8":"Or share the week itself with one person, who signs in and always sees the latest","902d572f22":"Turn the week into one picture for the group chat or the fridge, or share it with one person who signs in to see it.","267c1474f1":"A week for each child","6b1033c892":"Each child has their own week, and one for the term that’s coming.","d6e0ac237b":"A card to text or print","233ad6e643":"One picture with each day’s programs and pickup times, made on your phone.","97b32b3093":"Pick your school, then add a program to each afternoon.","0123457e99":"Send it to whoever does pickup, or stick it on the fridge.","99d1f692be":"{n} days off still to come this year","cad5bb6640":"Every day school is closed, covered","2545d86564":"Sam’s days off","1aec861d5e":"Every day school is closed this year is on the list, with who has posted a camp for each.","9f05ef7df6":"Every day off in order. Choose a camp or a day at home for each child, and tick a day once you’ve signed up.","2308bdae9f":"Green is signed up, yellow is still to sign up for, and a dashed day has no plan yet.","84c5af48fe":"The same plan on a month of squares, so a break with no plan yet stands out before it sneaks up on you.","8f95be3b1e":"Who’s open each day off","ddf2d28366":"A filled box means the program has posted a camp for that day. A dark one is in the plan.","8593b9fba7":"One chart of which programs have posted a camp for each day off. Tap a box and that day is in your plan.","7219dbf21f":"Signed up? Tick it off","560689cf6a":"Each camp day waits on a to-do list, with a link to the camp’s sign-up page, until you tick it.","ad84f3da53":"A calendar for the fridge","6481bb0de5":"One picture of every day off, to print or send to a sitter.","4970b73b0b":"Choose where each child will be on each day off.","389cc94cbc":"Tick off each camp as you sign up, and print the calendar.","b225fe2f2c":"{n} weeks of summer","ba9406a692":"The whole summer on one page","77d8595bc9":"Sam’s summer","28e9e1dd73":"Every week from the last day of school to Labor Day, with the camps that run in each and what the summer adds up to.","a8ac9a1114":"Every week from the last day of school to Labor Day. Add a camp to each one, and the plan adds up what the summer costs.","19f837128e":"Each camp sits on the days it runs, so an open week is easy to spot.","6490107658":"Month by month, with each camp on the days it runs and the open weeks easy to spot.","f87a087dc7":"When each camp runs","f7ce2f239d":"Each column is a week, named by its Monday. A dark box is in the plan.","f224f682db":"Which camps run which weeks, on one chart. Tap a box and that week is in your summer.","f8f59d7169":"See the gaps","32f8109e44":"A week with nothing on it stands out, in June rather than the Friday before.","06ae1e105d":"A summer for each child","a3a6542e2d":"Set an age and the camps narrow to the ones that take it.","0b4be3c8ff":"What the summer adds up to","01f01e7995":"A running total from the weekly prices the camps post.","53045ad71b":"Add a camp to each week, for one child or for each of them.","443de05966":"Print the summer, or put the weeks in your phone’s calendar.","ccee7d0831":"The week, the days off and the summer, in one place","d6e1878467":"Days off, camp weeks, sign-up dates and your own dates on one calendar, month by month.","c432e49f70":"A month at a time: days off, camp weeks, sign-up dates and the dates you add yourself.","f582e20e72":"Coming up","1d5afcb49d":"The whole year in date order, from this week to Labor Day.","5475c1fc92":"Or the same year as a list in date order, to read from the top down.","bd5c2b83f8":"Sign-up dates, lined up","679492d377":"Openings and deadlines for the programs and camps on your plans, on the days they happen.","a95490f10d":"Your own dates too","4817a9b383":"Picture day, a form that’s due: add them and they sit beside everything else.","237dfa0a21":"Private","62b6e2cdfa":"No link and no sharing. Only you can open it.","8e92e74052":"Build a week, plan the days off, plan the summer: any or all.","79493759e5":"Open one calendar and see the whole year.","3fbd5bd3b5":"What’s left to sign up for, in one list","9877f1d8e3":"Camps to sign up for","765a98f2ff":"Go to its sign-up page","37395c227d":"Signed up","e69c85aa2d":"Putting a camp on your plan doesn’t sign your child up. Each camp day waits here until you tick it.","aa5ba0d111":"Plan the days school is closed, and each camp day you pick lands here with a link to that camp’s own sign-up page. Tick it off once you’ve signed up.","d23b8c17cf":"Tick it off","1067b9e3f4":"A day leaves the list when you tick it, and turns green on your plan.","e39a21a9b3":"Straight to the sign-up page","e906a28ce7":"Each camp has a link to the page where it takes sign-ups.","b54e84d521":"Plan the days off: pick a camp for each day you need one.","a515bd1a85":"Sign up at each camp, and tick it off here.","c361ac4de5":"See it as","2b41c13112":"Make your plan","e41df9fa48":"Take it with you","b18e05123f":"It’s free for parents.","e320e6731a":"No password: we email you a code, or you use Google.","521b388f55":"Started a plan on this phone or computer before? Log in at the top of the page.","7bf39f5748":"The roster needs JavaScript turned on.","6058b0c1c4":"That link doesn’t open a week any more","a394925693":"Weeks used to be shared as a link that anyone could open. They aren’t now. Ask the person who sent it to share the week with your email address instead: you’ll get an invitation, and it will open once you sign in.","0833e5be5f":"Child’s name","8db5e54ac8":"A first name, a nickname or an initial. It shows on the roster you share, and it’s how your profile tells one child’s week from another’s.","f82be68a7f":"Week","7aeba4cd15":"Budget","14ec1581e9":"Make it a card","4d4ce73b15":"Card","3b6a3dd872":"Keep & share","09ca55ca52":"Share","ac858ab685":"Add a program","bd294d45de":"Roll a week","ab0838e5a7":"Search by name, or by what it is: music, chess, soccer, a neighborhood, your school.","2f3b5c55bc":"Browse","d0266a1192":"Not sure what to search for? Browse by what it is.","4a66d14807":"Everything","75a791fc13":"At or picking up from","d2b782f85f":"Neighborhood","04c5a7fd88":"Free only","581db2b0e9":"Pick a school and a theme, and we’ll fill Monday to Friday.","f2f3d66a79":"School","aecc49c153":"Grade","044cf1802b":"Optional. It skips programs that don’t take that grade.","1427b5e649":"Music Prodigy","c90aa2dfa6":"Music every day","86a5a74e84":"Mathlete","1dc0fe5012":"STEM, chess and homework help","7fa36d2ec9":"The Da Vinci","e597bfefbd":"Art, science and music","25eb2ddb65":"Move It or Lose It","d4b2f6138c":"On their feet all week","5996e63410":"Glitter and Glue","3db3056781":"Arts and crafts all week","6d7fc1d86e":"Bookworm","ee18507fe8":"Reading, writing and the library","c983e0a563":"Just for Fun","5eddf4e50b":"Games, play and rec time","aef69a3a46":"Wild Child","1ba73b8295":"Outside whenever possible","90bb48964e":"Jack of All Trades","d2534fc212":"Something different every day","571059a6c2":"A themed week is a starting point, picked at random from what’s listed for that school. Check days, ages and open spots with each program before you plan around it.","6209822bd5":"Drag a card by its colored top to move it to another day, or use the day buttons on the card.","35a6da7355":"Looks right? Make it a picture.","637080ff4f":"One card of the week to text to your partner, stick on the fridge or hand to a teacher.","8fd63544b7":"Share this schedule","32f0ed93d5":"What this roster costs","5b53065afb":"An estimate from each program’s published prices, for half a school year: 18 weeks of school, or five monthly bills. It leaves out registration fees, deposits, materials, sibling discounts, subsidies and financial aid. If you know what you’ll pay, add it to any line; it stays on this device. Confirm the price with each program before you budget on it.","ac085f0036":"One picture of the week to text, print, or hand to your child’s teacher, so they know where your child goes each day and who they are.","9c7696a8cb":"Who it’s for (optional)","a18fea4713":"A note (optional)","817e907c3b":"Your child’s photo (optional)","d03e72f9c9":"The photo never leaves this device. The card is made here in your browser, nothing is uploaded, and the photo isn’t saved.","ee82685bf6":"To email it to a teacher, share or save the card, then attach it to a message from your own email.","d5fe0a8fd9":"Want to keep this week too?","3a2b7f3ef2":"Save it to a free account so it’s on your phone and your computer, or share it with someone who signs in to see it.","121f62140c":"Save or share this week","743e0828a8":"Plan the days off too","7efefe9180":"Want next term’s sign-up dates before they open?","d63b67808e":"Get the dates by email.","86fa9d3efa":"Monday to Friday","8f3a8f4582":"Put a program on each afternoon and see the whole week in one place. More than one child? Each gets their own.","bd618a0f69":"Add programs day by day, or roll a themed week to start from","c616db0c7e":"See what the week comes to, from each program’s published prices","1eecb9c6f0":"Turn it into one picture to text, print, or hand to a teacher","7a81da9411":"{n} days off still to come","05ee33fa07":"Build your day-camp plan","e702195686":"Every day district schools are closed this year, and the {n} programs that run a camp on them.","178d270659":"See who’s open on each day off, break by break","c91aba10a7":"Pick a camp, or a day at home, for each child","b9a1cf59b7":"Save it as a calendar picture, or put the days in your phone’s calendar","c4d8f439a8":"Build your summer","8300c7278e":"The weeks between the last day of school and Labor Day, and which of {n} camps run in each one.","4972d8309b":"See on one chart which camps run each week","f4287b44cd":"Line up a camp for every week, child by child, and see what it adds up to","65dcbaa593":"Make it a calendar picture, or put the weeks in your phone’s calendar","80a1a206c1":"Plan your summer","b2227a3286":"With a free account","4adfdc18c7":"The three plans above, added up: the school week, every day off, the camp weeks and the sign-up dates, in date order for the whole year.","566de751c5":"One calendar file for your phone, which you can bring up to date later","fc1e4fd40e":"Room for your own dates: picture day, pretzel day, a form that’s due","c77ad2868f":"A picture of any month to send or print","bbecd22f31":"Private: it has no link, and only you can open it","e056c4f153":"Open my kids’ calendar","943b54f7fa":"Three planners, one for each part of a family’s year: the school week, the days school is closed, and the summer. All three are free: you sign in with a free account to use them.","5358c85b2b":"How the planners work","1248f9f60b":"Nothing to put on a plan yet?","748484767a":"to see what works with it, or","24cad23203":"look through every program","756fe30e51":"The planners need a free account. Signed in, each plan is kept in your profile, so it’s on every device you sign in on.","16240eaf31":"Days, hours and prices come from each program’s own website. Check with the program before you count on a spot.","1abe6064aa":"programs","0ff368cd6f":"Weekday afternoons once the bell rings: aftercare, music, art, sports, chess and more.","ec8bceb5f8":"See what’s at your child’s school, what picks up from it and what’s nearby","ac4714bc99":"Narrow the list by type, grade, neighborhood or day of the week","7f9b6db0a1":"Hours, cost, pickup and how to register, from each program’s own website","1ebc5e8730":"See all {n}, A to Z","2c7bed1aee":"Start from your school","324d2c4f8c":"places","4b4006d63b":"Saturday and Sunday classes: music, dance, art, skating, science. There’s no school pickup, so any child can sign up.","cc8a03bb87":"{sat} run on Saturdays, {sun} on Sundays","35e6292a6e":"The term, the times and the cost of each","5d34cf21a4":"Sorted by part of the city, so you can start close to home","7714bc4252":"See weekend classes","5cb71601bc":"Camps on the days district schools are closed: holidays, staff days, winter and spring break.","a79f395a83":"{n} days off still to come this school year","8e0ced1448":"Next one: {name}, {date}","6e99957da3":"See who’s open on each day, break by break","dbd50d4fa4":"See day-camp programs","6aef64103b":"camps","fabcc02131":"Day camps inside the city for the {n} weeks between the last day of school and Labor Day.","126664c498":"Ages, weeks, hours and prices, from each camp’s own website","3aaaea0493":"One chart of which camps run in each week","5d03839326":"Camps usually post next summer between December and March","05e88d0a6e":"See summer camps","ee4eabe00a":"Everything listed on this site, sorted by the kind of program it is. Pick the part of the year you’re filling, then narrow it down from there.","8329c3b1e3":"A place can be in more than one group: one that runs weekday afternoons, Saturday classes and camps on days off is counted in each.","ae608fb936":"After-school programs, by what they do","50760ff161":"Or narrow it another way","d7b8e86ea4":"What’s at your child’s school, what picks up from it and what’s nearby. Clubs a school runs for its own students are on that school’s page.","754d6bda83":"What’s based near home, and who comes to pick up.","d4678aa638":"By grade","eea904e13c":"Everything that takes your child’s grade.","1ff8a5bec8":"About these lists","21c16af351":"Every list is free to look through, and none of them needs an account.","869996becb":"Know one that’s missing?","0d1fc1aeaa":"Suggest a program","1758356db2":"or","ae2f739d19":"suggest a camp","fa141c259e":"Each column is a day district schools are closed. A filled box means the program’s own site lists a camp that day. The chart scrolls sideways.","3256dd3f29":"Tap a box to put that day in your plan.","10f50270e6":"Camp posted","2b9e7b7ed1":"In your plan","55f8e70fe1":"Choose where each child will be on every day school is closed, see who’s open on each, and tick off each camp as you sign up.","997f30f482":"Your days off","2c9a96711f":"Choose where each child will be on each day school is closed. Your picks are saved on this device and in your profile, so they’re there on your other devices.","cf3f7d3d6c":"First name (optional)","1e0e10baa0":"Kept with the plan in your profile. A nickname or an initial is fine.","5741e56a54":"Age (optional)","b378c7f722":"Shows the camps that take that age. Stays on this device.","23154df2fb":"Day by day","effd273d9b":"Pick your visual mode!","a1fffaaafb":"List","adab5090ac":"Calendar","701c483f81":"Grid","b2aea9acf3":"Share/Save","1c415d66eb":"Pick a camp or a day at home first. Then this is where you share the plan, add it to your calendar, make a picture of it and keep it in your profile.","93a713d780":"Make it a calendar","1c38cce747":"One picture of every day off, or a calendar for each month, to print for the fridge or send to a sitter. Every child with a day planned is on it.","768e0c1c69":"Title","43381a8514":"A photo (optional)","25ff2a2f1c":"The photo never leaves this device. The calendar is made here in your browser, nothing is uploaded, and the photo isn’t saved.","b511eb903f":"Every day off this year, and who runs camps","2aa3a370f7":"Dates come from each program’s own website. Check with the program before you count on a spot.","723abfff03":"School’s closed. What now?","4703b569d5":"Who runs a camp or a full day when district schools are closed, by neighborhood, and every day off this year.","32a16719a4":"The days","8422b24994":"Who runs something when school is closed","b48a619950":"{n} listed programs say they run camps or full days on days off. Children from any school can go, so start from your part of the city. {m} of them had no dates on their site when we checked, so ask which days they cover.","a1f2933bbb":"Days off still to come","28eb0e1ebe":"These are the School District of Philadelphia’s dates. A program is counted only when its own site lists that date.","4cf956e40d":"Plan each day off","ce6f6711c8":"Choose where each child will be on each day school is closed, as a list or on a calendar, and tick each camp off as you sign up.","5266119c26":"Before you count on it","b9eff86fb0":"Expect to drop your child off. Several programs say there is no school pickup on a day school is closed.","939ba83ac9":"A camp day is usually booked and paid for on its own, separate from after-school.","23f3e9d859":"The district’s calendar lists no early-dismissal days for students this year. If your school sends children home early, ask the program what it does.","25eceb785b":"Charter schools keep their own calendars, so their days off can differ from these.","bc3d3a20ad":"Know a program that runs on days off and isn’t here?","c2b3a35adc":"Save to your plan for {day}","af9fb423f5":"Sign up on the camp’s site","284b494835":"Full listing","a887a34c48":"Days off from school","4b0553114e":"{name}: camps for the day off","916c83cb8b":"Philadelphia’s district schools are closed on {when}.","42a081edea":"{n} programs listed here have posted a camp for it.","49d75bd6c3":"Open that day","cb14919d0e":"A program is listed here only when its own website names this date. Spots fill, so check with the program before you count on one.","5101f6a93d":"Looking for a particular camp?","b7e32adf5f":"Plan this day for each child","a6c33c5afe":"All days off this year","c7c92931bb":"Run camps on days off, with this one not posted","dc36506254":"These programs run camps on some days school is closed. Their sites didn’t list this date when we checked, so ask.","95f48d8b7a":"Before you book","fb7a0ef46e":"These are the School District of Philadelphia’s dates. Charter and private schools set their own calendars, so check yours.","51e514aa41":"Hours, prices and ages are on each program’s own page. Confirm with the program before you count on a spot.","e5a7c6a4b5":"Want a heads-up before each day off?","246e2086db":"Get them by email.","8d086594a2":"Save to your plan for the break","541d1ca8de":"{name}: camps for the break","39c81d8755":"Philadelphia’s district schools are closed from {when}.","2d43903477":"One program listed here has posted a camp for it.","da6637fb34":"Open during the break","cc9e934d79":"Plan the break for each child","44e91e5e1f":"Summer camps in Philadelphia","1340bb3f65":"Day camps inside the city, with the ages, weeks, hours and prices each camp posts on its own site.","a306f0d8b7":"Most of what’s here is from summer {year}, shown as a guide.","2231b0eb6b":"Camps usually post next summer between December and March. Each listing changes to {year} when its camp posts dates and prices, and says so on its card.","6c10526de4":"Waiting on one camp? Its page has a box to be emailed when it posts.","26e0ca0aa1":"Grades here are worked out from each camp’s ages, so check the ages on the camp’s page. Each camp has its own page with everything it posts.","d8a720ac98":"Camps we haven’t been able to read yet","e65614e566":"These run day camps in the city too. Their details go up once we’ve read them on the camp’s own site.","028d1e3e42":"Suggest a camp","72ab82a2ab":"Know a city day camp that isn’t here? Send its name and its website, and we’ll read it and add it.","3ba73d32cf":"I run a camp","743141e3ff":"Listings come from each camp’s public pages and are not endorsements. Dates, prices and openings change, so confirm with the camp before you plan around it.","3979b00c23":"Run this camp?","94cd12d67e":"Plan your summer, week by week","67d32633d0":"Camps close to this one","bf38cb71fc":"{n} weeks between the last day of school and Labor Day. See which camps run each week, and line up your own summer.","2630f3292e":"Most of these dates are from summer {year}, shown as a guide.","8bcce75ac4":"A camp that hasn’t posted {next} yet is shown on the weeks it ran last summer, moved to the same week of the calendar. Camps usually post between December and March, and each one switches to its real dates when it does.","20c7d1ed6f":"Your summer","13c91fbc33":"Add a camp to each week, for one child or for each of them. Your picks are saved on this device and in your profile, so they’re there on your other devices.","1464c87cf3":"Age this summer (optional)","c44edd8ef9":"Week by week","8109bc56db":"Add a camp to a week first. Then this is where you share the summer, add it to your calendar, make a picture of it and keep it in your profile.","07f65ead39":"One picture of the whole summer, or a calendar for each month, to print for the fridge or send to family. Every child with a camp picked is on it.","cf5610a79d":"Each column is a week, named by its Monday. A filled box means the camp listed that week. The chart scrolls sideways and down.","e615da79f1":"Tap a box to add that week to your summer.","b387b496c0":"{year} dates","3303fccc81":"{year} dates, as a guide","f1473f7521":"In your summer","c5a4c226c5":"No dates listed yet","0ee69f223b":"These camps haven’t put dates we can chart on their sites. You can still add one to any week in the list, then check with the camp.","0930275c37":"Every camp, with ages, hours and prices","1329f04e9e":"Which camps run each week of summer {year}","0549a5029b":"{n} weeks between the last day of school and Labor Day, and which of {m} camps has listed each one.","15c6ab3df9":"These camps haven’t put dates we can chart on their sites. Ask each one which weeks it runs.","06b981cf5b":"Line up your own summer","064faabcf9":"Add a camp to each week, for one child or for each of them, and see what the summer adds up to.","04b3cb45ce":"My kids’ calendar","b441742617":"Everything you’ve planned for the school year and the summer, in one place: the after-school week, every day off, camp weeks and sign-up dates. Only you can see it.","9b0d784c99":"The calendar needs JavaScript turned on.","79e8062221":"The same account opens the planners:","43560280c5":"build a week","bbce9be21c":"plan the days off","52b7fa5bee":"plan the summer","808737672b":"Getting your calendar…","109448d45c":"The year","90c75b6d90":"Add it","34099240ab":"Your calendar fills in from your planners, and from any dates you add here yourself.","9dc1f228e8":"Add your own dates","0d42ee85c5":"Picture day, pretzel day, a form that’s due, a half day: anything you need to remember, for one child or for everyone. They show up in the calendar below, in the pictures and in the file for your phone. Something that happens every week needs only the day of the week.","97211a8888":"What","bd88489720":"How often","769bb19e61":"When","905471c963":"Which day","ab772c4da0":"Who it’s for","1b995e4f5d":"Add several at once","4a2dd00d19":"Type or paste one on each line, starting with the date or the weekday. They go to whoever is picked under “Who it’s for”.","2e81b307fb":"Dates, one on each line","b4db80b87b":"A weekly one repeats until the last day of school and skips the days school is closed. Your own dates are kept on this device only: they aren’t sent to us, so add them on the phone or computer you’ll look at.","81ae07a7ca":"View it","b96ddaab20":"Your plan","2bc6b5e359":"Make it a picture","2c04ce6cc7":"A calendar for each month, to print for the fridge or send to family. It’s made here in your browser.","991cf872b0":"Show the dates I added, on every month they fall in","a69abc716e":"Pencil it in","6c60d61caa":"Add it to your calendar","ec12bceffe":"One file with everything ticked below, for the calendar on your phone or computer. Open it and your calendar app adds the entries. It’s a copy: if a date changes later, this page will say so, and you download it again.","b8454c2ccb":"What goes in the file","fdd25e589c":"Days off, with each child’s plan","0f17007d7b":"Summer camp weeks","70e7f1bf95":"Camps still showing last summer’s weeks, as a guide","fd241c6103":"Sign-up dates","00c5347c68":"The after-school week, repeating every school week","e70625a046":"Dates you added yourself","bf93492c8b":"A to-do list for camp sign-ups","8665aed362":"To do","3493d3bb61":"The camp days you’ve planned and haven’t signed up for yet, in one list. It’s part of a free account.","debcf8243f":"What’s left to sign up for. Putting a camp on your plan doesn’t sign your child up, so every camp day you’ve planned waits here until you tick it off.","2414a38581":"The to-do list needs JavaScript turned on.","e019511391":"Getting your list…","e830a45284":"How this list works","f53423e041":"It’s made from your days-off plan: every day you’ve put a camp on, for every child. A day at home needs no sign-up, so it isn’t here.","1be022cc9d":"A tick is your own note. We can’t see whether you registered, and the camp isn’t told anything.","397ffe942b":"Ticks are kept with the plan, on this device and in your profile, so they follow you to another phone or computer.","b6c6729938":"Change the camp on a day and its tick is cleared, because it’s a new sign-up.","9264c1c2d3":"Saturday and Sunday classes","f962aaaf9d":"Weekend classes for kids across the city: what runs, on which day, and where. Open one for its term, times and cost.","ea126e4246":"Looking for a particular class?","bfd62374ec":"A weekend class has no school pickup, so this list goes by where the class is. Any child can sign up, whichever school they go to.","fa6409c2a5":"This covers the programs already on this site, plus weekend-only places from a first sweep of the city. It isn’t every class in Philadelphia, and some listed programs run weekend classes that their sites don’t spell out by day, so ask.","363c044f46":"Know a weekend class that should be here?","c32870d51a":"The dates, before they sneak up on you","1c9bab1f23":"Sign-up openings, deadlines and days off for your school, by email. Sign-up dates come the morning after they’re posted here, and days off in a {day} round-up.","6ecdc6499c":"Pick your school and follow it. If you’re new, signing in takes a minute: an email address and a 6-digit code.","77d81956df":"Where should they go?","aae5d56166":"Pick your school, then leave your first name and an email address. That’s the whole form.","cd5afd9aa8":"Your school","ca195c3360":"every school on the site","bfe862f18f":"A school that isn’t listed yet","ab11b57cad":"What you’ll get","dca1fbab07":"A heads-up when sign-ups open or a deadline is close at a program that serves your school.","3900e33c7c":"Each district day off at least {n} days ahead, with the listed programs running a camp that day.","193afb6b51":"Sign-up news can come on any morning, so you don’t find out after the spots are gone. If your school isn’t listed yet, you get the days off and every listed program’s dates.","a6d743c0bb":"Waiting on one program? Each program’s page has a “Tell me when sign-ups open” box, for emails about that program alone.","fb894a5f1a":"Waiting on a summer camp? Each camp’s page has a box to be emailed when it posts next summer or names a sign-up day.","019bcc12cb":"It runs on a free account, so you can see and change what you follow. No questions about your children.","ade5beae79":"Dates coming up","b98fe6f034":"Stop emails about one thing","df65e4b3b0":"You only hear about what you follow. Stop one and the rest carry on.","1fe52884f2":"This page needs JavaScript turned on. You can also sign in and stop following from your profile.","ad5d75607a":"One moment…","db8ec9b83c":"To see or change everything you follow,","d09e164f4f":"sign in to your account","af7d2450d4":"The Unsubscribe link at the foot of any email stops every email from us, including news about the site.","5607151fb2":"How did it go?","2ac3b3b289":"A first-hand note from one family helps the next one choose. Every review is read before it’s posted.","ce536c2876":"Which program?","68730f575a":"Your child’s school","83cd624d2e":"Your rating","501c17289a":"Your review","665f7e8d69":"What was pickup like? Homework help? Would you sign up again?","8ee9829c7e":"Your first name","da1f043fb7":"Shown with your review.","2354db7577":"Never shown. Only used if we need to confirm something.","16add200f8":"This is my own experience as a parent or caregiver.","f4cfa14ce9":"Send review","48216a08c6":"House rules","568a415161":"First-hand only. Write about what your own family experienced.","1f0a3f8568":"Be specific and fair. Details help more than adjectives.","3f759500a1":"No names of children or individual staff.","21eeea0c1a":"Programs can’t review themselves.","8382938cc6":"Reviews show your first name and school, and appear after they’ve been read. Nobody pays to have a review posted or removed.","c35f6fbdee":"Thank you. It’s in.","65cb4c318e":"Your review will appear once it’s been read.","7a6310ea7e":"This jawn isn’t here","8e5ad16e04":"The link may be old, or the page moved.","8d980d5757":"Start from the list of schools.","94a8184560":"Log in to your account","4ab2910209":"Your account","cb9c4347e9":"Your school, your plans and your kids’ calendar for the year, on any device. There’s no password to remember.","b81f2e17e0":"New here?","5be180b534":"This is where you change things: your name, email address and phone number, your school and grades, what you’re emailed about, what you follow, and who you share with.","6efbd57efc":"Accounts need JavaScript turned on.","191885e234":"What an account gives you","f704f50512":"See the whole year in one calendar.","7e0b221398":"“My kids’ calendar” puts the school week, every day off, the camp weeks and each sign-up date in date order. Only you can open it.","f892383e6e":"Put it on your phone.","79cc69953b":"One calendar file for the year that you can bring up to date, and a picture of any month for the fridge.","384f921908":"Follow and save.","d29abae63f":"Follow a program, a camp or your school and its sign-up dates come by email. Save favorites to find them again.","d3a0950676":"Share a week with one person.","4523317b1d":"A grandparent or a sitter signs in to see it, and you can take it back.","31599229ab":"Share with a small group.","b7da72d2a0":"A few families you invite by email see each other’s weeks. Nobody else can find the group or ask to join.","824f173880":"It’s free. The plans you make are kept in your profile, so they’re on your phone and your computer, and you can delete the account whenever you like.","6cb0c01f74":"Making an account means you agree to the","f137c5ff1a":"terms of use","89edaa0208":"Run a program or camp?","4b2b4e230b":". It’s the same account.","733d535919":"What an account keeps, and who sees it","aecdd1c338":"Your profile keeps the plans you make: a child’s first name with their week, days off and summer, and your school. No last names, addresses, notes or photos.","0dea7d9d59":"A shared week opens only for the email address you sent it to, once that person has signed in. It can’t be searched for, and its link shows nothing to anyone else.","d05870eaa7":"You can take a week back, stop sharing, or delete your account at any time. Shared weeks delete themselves when the school year ends.","2888e0b6c6":"The full details are on the privacy page.","d634af0382":"Create your free account","367962819d":"Keep every plan you build, the school week, the days off and the summer, and see them together in one private calendar for the whole year. It takes about a minute, and there’s no password to remember.","40587bfc25":"Log in to see your profile","31d0394e59":"Your school, what you follow, your favorites and your plans, on any device. There’s no password to remember.","bed4c69e3f":"Everything in your account, on one card. To change any of it, go to your account.","37e31607b2":"Your profile needs JavaScript turned on.","6157136701":"Your group","390afd21ce":"Only the people invited to this group can see it.","1020e6eb49":"Groups need JavaScript turned on.","26dba34241":"Open your invitation","5db9909bea":"Someone shared a week with you or invited you to a group. Sign in with the email address the invitation was sent to: it only opens for that address.","5bf1f25f73":"Joining a group needs JavaScript turned on.","b0a8b36607":"What gets shared","64db7cc525":"A child’s first name and the programs on their week. No last names, addresses, notes or photos.","e94cfe6c62":"Only the people invited by email address can see it. Its link shows nothing to anyone else.","afbfa1f299":"If you add your own child’s week to a group, you can take it back out, leave the group or delete your account at any time.","6ff93ce468":"Run a program or camp? Claim your listing.","b4cef1b42e":"Find your program below and claim it with your work email. Then keep its dates, costs and hours up to date yourself. It’s free, and it takes a couple of minutes.","5cd372bd2a":"Claiming a listing needs JavaScript turned on.","237e65d7ff":"What claiming gets you","6c6a68b6bd":"Your listing is already on the site, and parents are already reading it. Claim it and it becomes yours to keep right.","769128eff3":"Keep your dates current.","fe74e3dcea":"Post sign-up openings, deadlines, term dates and camp days as soon as you set them, instead of waiting for us to find them.","0624398afc":"Say whether there’s space.","2a7ed3b1a9":"Mark your listing “Spots open”, “Waitlist” or “Full”. It shows to parents straight away, with the date.","4e889a80a4":"See your numbers.","ef53688255":"How many times your listing was opened this month, how many clicks went on to your sign-up page and website, and how many families put you on a plan.","59d55500b1":"Show parents it’s kept up.","6cef4c3b17":"A “Claimed” mark tells them the listing is looked after by the people who run it.","0a491a101d":"Maple Street Arts Club","1677cca133":"Painting, clay and printmaking after school, with pickup from two schools","308e17d220":"Art","7e15a1e710":"Grades","4374aaee24":"to","c9c417e40a":"Spots open","f6db3475e5":"as of Oct 6","9e25a34e63":"Hours","e5dace639c":"Monday to Thursday, dismissal to 6 pm","64ae43e8fe":"Cost","2811ea058e":"$95 a week, with a sibling discount","842b7b5d71":"Dates","51b3d09b4f":"Winter term sign-up opens November 12","4f05cd6409":"Add to calendar","0b81497c85":"Sign up","c670957813":"Checked October 6.","1b62794de3":"Only you see this","f8228be674":"Your listing, last 30 days","6bb687226b":"times your listing was opened","b2d90aedca":"clicks to sign up","59541d4684":"times it was put on a family’s plan","69f384a9c1":"An example of a claimed listing. The program and its numbers are made up.","043ada32ba":"Want more on your listing?","1583d46ab1":"A premium listing adds photos and your logo, a section in your own words, an offer or event line, a button parents use to send you a question, and month-by-month numbers. The listing itself stays free; premium is the extras.","20144626cd":"See what premium adds","67bf02dabe":"From {price} a month. Claim your listing first; premium is added to it.","cbbfac7f02":"Find your listing.","1b5a2a50f1":"Search by name above. Every program and summer camp on the site is there.","bd5f48aa2a":"Sign in with your work email.","5a343478c1":"It has to be an address at your program’s own website: if the listing’s website is example.org, an address ending in @example.org. That is how we know you speak for it. If the addresses match, the claim stands straight away.","028587cbea":"Send changes when something moves.","0e10b31324":"New dates, a new price, new hours. We read each one and update the listing, usually within a few days.","79fc372dc7":"Good to know","1d92e2bf83":"A personal address (Gmail, Yahoo and so on) can’t claim a listing, even if it’s the one printed on your flyer. We have no way to tell it apart from anyone else’s.","301c1fb7c9":"“Continue with Google” works if your work email is a Google account at your program’s address. A personal Gmail account will sign you in, but it can’t claim anything.","df57559f10":"Some listings sit on a website many people share: a city rec center, a school’s clubs, a program inside a university. Those claims wait for us to say yes, and we may write to ask a question first.","83f5e887bb":"Parents see a “Claimed” mark on the listing. Your name and email address are never shown.","eeda369117":"A claim doesn’t change what the listing says by itself. Changes you send are looked at by a person, then published.","c44909adfd":"Listings are free and stay free. Nobody pays to be listed or to be ranked higher.","66918d5568":"Want more on yours?","c729af8fcf":"A premium listing adds photos, your own words and offers.","114d2e3383":"Not on the site yet?","cb59876413":"Suggest your program","bcb356b14f":"your camp","bf7c4a20c3":", with its website, and claim it once it’s up.","31fedd6838":"What we keep about a claim is on the privacy page.","f152d8ba1b":"Photos and your logo","b023ab3ddd":"Up to six photos and a logo, at the top of your listing.","b6ba27d757":"An offer or event line","340b97e172":"An open house, a trial class, early-bird pricing. It shows near the top until the date you set.","bdfe18faff":"A section in your own words","acabca628f":"Say what makes your program yours, the way you’d say it to a parent on a tour.","df74e9174d":"A button for questions","3aaa8bae19":"Parents send a question from your listing and it lands in your inbox, with their address to reply to.","c5fabc3736":"Fuller numbers","f0623eb40d":"Month by month: how often your listing was opened, how many families follow it or saved it, and which schools they come from. Numbers only, never who.","5c28ba3223":"A flyer to print","469cde181f":"With a code that opens your listing, for the front desk or the school fair.","b5020eb904":"From the program","edf83cde87":"Open house on November 12 at 6 pm. Come see the studio and meet the teachers.","667dbf96fc":"In their own words","8caf71cd62":"Written by Maple Street Arts Club, not by us.","4d93204824":"We keep groups small, so every kid gets their hands in the clay. Most afternoons end with something to carry home.","cf94bdf391":"Ask a question","187ac43115":"Your listing, month by month","6faec47b65":"A flyer with your listing’s code, ready to print","938c2e84cd":"An example of a premium listing. The program, its schools and its numbers are made up.","1ae5e802c8":"Premium listings","478b084c0d":"Your listing on {site} is free, and it stays free. Premium adds your photos, your words and your offers to it, and shows you what families do with it.","59bd1ff6f9":"What it costs","7622eb5aa4":"Yearly","fbe0b376ca":"a year","ac7bb6bf3d":"{n} months free, compared with paying by the month.","8173c2a946":"Best value","d31edb7b8a":"Monthly","1f6df70edf":"a month","0e667fa69a":"Pay as you go.","60c8c94f34":"This is the founding price, for the first programs to sign up. It stays yours for as long as you stay signed up. Later, premium will cost {m} a month or {y} a year.","977a68d4ad":"Sign up your listing","2271dc3c5a":"Run a free program, a school club or a rec center?","d57e339ca8":"Write to us before you sign up.","7578f1ab32":"What premium adds","86ad675b99":"Signing up needs JavaScript turned on.","b43a8e1ca6":"What premium doesn’t do","7ff436f1ae":"It doesn’t move you up. Listings are never ordered by who pays, and premium doesn’t change where yours appears.","920cd53cfc":"It doesn’t replace your free listing. Claiming it, sending corrections and saying whether you have space all stay free, with or without premium.","1f2156cfd8":"It never costs families anything. Parents don’t pay for any part of this site.","d6aee5b29e":"Nothing you add goes up unread. A person looks at each photo, section and offer line before it shows on your listing.","ea93e96569":"It doesn’t lock you in. You can stop at any time: write to us and we’ll end it.","0050852efc":"What we keep about a claim and a premium listing is on the privacy page.","df316e17de":"…","62d6f827b0":"{from} shared “{group}” with you on {site}: the after-school programs their child goes to each day.","ccb9cf3374":"To see it, open this link and sign in with this email address ({email}):","8989b05c55":"If it asks for a code:","9b72450db2":"It only opens for this address, and it shows a first name and programs. If you don’t know {name}, ignore this email.","477d69efa9":"{name} shared “{group}” with you","b80f5ebdc2":"{from} shared the after-school programs their child goes to each day.","e1e85bd8a4":"Sign in with this email address ({email}).","6463a7f86e":"See the week","2e9720e69a":"{name} shared “{group}” with you on {site}","a5e0f5ea98":"{from} invited you to the group “{group}” on {site}, to share your children’s after-school weeks with each other.","e4a43b5806":"To join, open this link and sign in with this email address ({email}):","d188c0e8de":"Only invited addresses can join, and a group shows first names and programs only. If you don’t know {name}, ignore this email: nothing happens unless you join.","0bf3b112bf":"{name} invited you to “{group}”","1c0ce4e141":"{from} invited you to a private group, to share your children’s after-school weeks with each other.","6aee0bf93a":"Join the group","eb4a565f17":"{name} invited you to “{group}” on {site}","cf5676f7a3":"You get this because you manage a listing on {site}.","69a2543991":"To stop the emails about your listing:","fbbaa2f098":"Stop the emails about your listing","a069c5256a":"Your answer about space has run out, so parents no longer see one.","8e08fe22a1":"Parents can see on your listing whether you have room.","7e88992ebd":"Say whether there are spots, a waitlist or no room. It takes one tap and stays up for {days} days.","e887d930de":"Say if there’s space","01fe6c9bdc":"No sign-up date is posted on your listing. Families who follow it are reminded the day before a date and that morning, so send in your next one.","8c01c2a680":"Send in a date","8df09b43f2":"Your listing has no reviews yet. The managers page has a link, and a message you can copy, to send to your families.","3fe23fa281":"Ask for a review","0b3b831ec9":"Something new this term? Propose a change to your listing and it goes up once it has been checked.","b144036b2d":"Update your listing","01c27eeb5f":"Its page was opened {times} in the last 30 days ({before} in the 30 before).","2a3ebd4e5e":"Its page was opened {times} in the last 30 days.","ff66c7dc26":"{n} to sign up","09383be717":"{n} to your website","6524e5adfb":"put on a family’s plan {n}","527cf6d98d":"{n} asked for its emails","21b3f467c6":"{n} sent to you","87ea7db4a4":"Also:","fbe66e09b2":"{n} new reviews of {listing} were published on {site}.","85549999a7":"A new review of {listing} was published on {site}.","2debe6297b":"Reviews are read before they go up, and the people who run a listing have no say over them. If one gets a fact wrong, reply to this email.","49d4a92be7":"New reviews of {listing}","baaa7f84ee":"A new review of {listing}","b0853600a7":"Read the reviews","5bb19c6b76":"Read the review","1bb469ff87":"Hi {first},","ec6fd691ee":"Here is how your listing did on {site}.","abc4d0ad94":"Here is how your listings did on {site}.","445e524ad4":"One thing to do for {listing}:","dabf80ab0b":"One thing to do:","b9c78f61ee":"A premium listing","6bee40edb8":"adds photos, your own words, an offer line and month-by-month numbers.","d101df0cd7":"Your listing this month: {listing}","e6d6509023":"Your listings this month: {listing} and {more} more","85559f1893":"{n} started following {listing} this week.","b22211adeb":"They hear about its sign-up dates by email or as a notification on their phone, so it’s worth keeping the dates on your listing current.","784347f58c":"New followers for {listing}","9302561aa2":"Open your listing’s tools","b7f3a82bc8":"A question about {listing} on {site}:","1a063da6fc":"Reply to this email, or open your listing’s tools and propose a change, and the listing is updated once it has been checked. Nothing on it changes until you answer.","1ac9748532":"A question about {listing}","06d54757a0":"Sign in to {site}","3eb45df396":"Open this link on the device you want to sign in on:","9e7824a66b":"Tap the button on the device you want to sign in on.","be86d1c0ed":"Or type this code into the page that asked for it: {code}","a282f155d8":"Both work once and stop working after {minutes} minutes. If you didn’t ask for this, ignore it: nobody can sign in without this email.","ada2e9e96f":"Sign in","fabd45a780":"Your sign-in link for {site}","123741ec0a":"Use this address for your {site} account","59bfea32e2":"Someone signed in to a {site} account asked to use this email address for it. If that was you, type this code into the account page:","ac34bf8f8e":"It works once and stops working after {minutes} minutes. If it wasn’t you, ignore this: nothing changes without the code.","d2e2d957c3":"Use this address for your account","50a434d6bb":"Your code to change your {site} email address","92480d1bb4":"The email address on your {site} account was changed.","a3fb9ee55e":"Your {site} account now signs in with a different address, and this one is no longer on it. If you did this, there’s nothing to do.","d3330079a4":"If you didn’t, write to {contact} straight away.","4def93d89b":"Your account’s email address was changed","fb7c96f629":"Your {site} email address was changed","c9a3d1d975":"{name} asked a question on your {site} listing for “{listing}”:","42a2e5dffd":"{name} asked on your listing:","ffbde3d45a":"Reply to this email to answer them at {email}.","ac47f77339":"This came from the “Ask a question” button on your listing. {site} passed it along and did not keep a copy.","6cd1562546":"A question about {listing} from a parent","8f1ace299b":"(viewing only)","314f67afbf":"{name} joined {group}","a8177e0a81":"{name} joined your group “{group}” on {site}, from the address you invited ({email}).","dc3b58a786":"If that isn’t who you expected, remove them here:","7174c8faf2":"{name} joined your group from the address you invited ({email}). If that isn’t who you expected, you can remove them.","a7fd7e22e5":"Open the group","f6988f3f88":"You’re getting this because you made this group on {site}.","8f68142d77":"You’re in: {group}","5563b54305":"You’ve been approved to see “{group}” on {site}.","fda79e8c1c":"You’ve been approved. You can see the group’s weeks now.","a2a4ece329":"You’re getting this because you asked to join this group on {site}."}
